stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> StartingUp
    StartingUp --> Idle : startup modes written
    StartingUp --> ExitingOnError : startup write fails or terminal closes
    Idle --> TurnRunning : user sends prompt
    TurnRunning --> Idle : turn finishes
    Idle --> WritingFrame : frame flush starts
    TurnRunning --> WritingFrame : frame flush starts
    WritingFrame --> Idle : frame written (no turn)
    WritingFrame --> TurnRunning : frame written (turn active)
    WritingFrame --> ExitingOnError : frame write fails
    Idle --> ExitingOnError : input closes, EIO, or alt-screen write fails
    TurnRunning --> ExitingOnError : input closes, EIO, or alt-screen write fails
    Idle --> SpinningRevoked : macOS tty revoked (current / no_pollnval)
    SpinningRevoked --> SpinningRevoked : poll ignores POLLNVAL [breaks NoSpin]
    StartingUp --> ClosedQuietly : SIGHUP arrives
    Idle --> ClosedQuietly : SIGHUP arrives or user quits
    TurnRunning --> ClosedSavingTurn : SIGHUP arrives
    ExitingOnError --> ClosedQuietly : classified as hang-up (no turn)
    ExitingOnError --> ClosedSavingTurn : classified as hang-up (turn active)
    ExitingOnError --> ErrorShownWrongly : terminal gone missed [breaks GoneIsQuiet]
    ExitingOnError --> ErrorShownRightly : terminal still open and owned
    ClosedQuietly --> [*]
    ClosedSavingTurn --> [*]
    ErrorShownWrongly --> [*]
    ErrorShownRightly --> [*]
    note right of ErrorShownWrongly
        Shortest path (current):
        StartingUp -> ExitingOnError (terminal closed) -> ErrorShownWrongly
    end note
    note right of SpinningRevoked
        Shortest path (current):
        StartingUp -> Idle (tty revoked) -> SpinningRevoked -> SpinningRevoked
    end note
